Package: arc-rebar
Version: 1.0.3
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: pciutils, initramfs-tools
Suggests: vulkan-tools, mesa-opencl-icd, ocl-icd-libopencl1, gcc, make
Maintainer: Rod Burlamaqui <RodBurlamaqui@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/RodBurlamaqui/Intel-ARC-Rebar
Description: Resizable BAR for Intel Arc GPUs on firmware without ReBAR support
 Enables the full VRAM aperture of Intel Arc (Battlemage / Alchemist) discrete
 GPUs on motherboards whose firmware has no Resizable BAR option, without
 modifying firmware. Runs from the initramfs before the GPU driver binds.
 .
 Installing this package enables NOTHING by itself. Run 'arc-rebar diagnose',
 then 'arc-rebar install' to enable it after safety checks and acceptance of
 the licence and disclaimer.
 .
 Also ships read-only diagnostics under /usr/share/arc-rebar/diag
 ('arc-rebar diag <tool>'): which PCIe link is real, which bridge BAR0 pins the
 root port window, Vulkan heap interpretation, the real OpenCL allocation
 ceiling, GPU health.
 .
 Proprietary licence: personal, non-commercial use free of charge;
 commercial and enterprise use requires separate licensing (including
 hardware, driver and OS vendors). See /usr/share/doc/arc-rebar/copyright.
